    "expectedRule": "Chapter 12 has three clause desks (body 肉身, memory 记忆, return 归返). The first clear of a desk leaves a pending clause that blocks leaving with `终稿条款尚未裁定，请先选择认证或删改。`; law/resolve-redaction-clause certifies for free or redacts for max(1, floor(maxHp x 8%)) HP. Max HP is derived from the build (the decoder recomputes it, so no HP is given as input): 50 + 14 x body 50 + patched_coat 10 = 760. A redaction therefore costs 60. Display: title 删界终稿, status `抉择 r/3，认证 c，删改 d[，待裁定 <clause>]，预估|冻结条款 k/3`; severity resolved once all three are resolved or frozen, danger while pending, otherwise warning; meter {resolved, 3}; targetReached when all are resolved and nothing is pending. Each clause sector (memory: north_clue_cache/upper_supply_margin -> memory_survey_archive; return: south_clue_cache/lower_supply_margin -> return_revision_portal; body: palimpsest_censor_alpha/upper_revision_portal -> body_proof_vault) opens only for a certified clause; a redacted one stays closed with `对应条款必须选择认证；删改后该选区永久关闭。`. The four boss approaches need all three clauses resolved (`肉身、记忆与归返三份条款全部裁定后开放。`). Selecting the boss freezes the choices; in the sealed boss encounter a certified body clause gives the boss +10% defense, a certified memory clause +10% art power, a certified return clause -10% healing and -10% guard effect, a redacted clause nothing (no entry passives here). The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
